+The Japanese figure needs care. It belongs to an AVQI version 03.01 validation
+for Japanese that this reference has not yet obtained. A separate paper by the
+same group validated AVQI version **02.02** in Japanese and reports a threshold
+of 3.15, with sensitivity 72.5% and specificity 95.2%, on a standardized
+syllable number of 22 [@hosokawa2017avqi]. The two are not rival estimates:
+they belong to different versions of the index, with different regression
+weights and different speech-material lengths, so 3.15 cannot be compared with
+any threshold in @tbl-avqi-thresholds. Always pair an AVQI threshold with its
+version.
